==Strategy==
The difficulty of the stage comes from the amount of times your units pierce the Possessed Empress' [[Shield]]. Because her Shield has a whopping ''1.2 million'' HP and regenerates up to 9 times, attempting to brute-force this stage is out of the question. The stage also spawns plenty of hard-pushing peons, which requires units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to swiftly deal with without losing too much ground. Most of the time you'll be cycling between killing the peons, breaking Possessed Empress' Shield with units like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] or [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]], knocking back the Empress, and repeat. When Possessed Empress lands an attack, she sends out a level 5 [[Mini-Wave]] that [[Slow]]s all of your units, making it extremely difficult for your units to catch up to the front line, which allows for the enemies to move closer to your [[Cat Base]]. Bringing [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can help a lot in preventing all of your units from being Slowed.

Having Can Can Cat's [[Money Up]] [[Talents|Talent]] is amazing here, as the stage doesn't provide too much cash.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Especially with their Double Bounty Talent, they are quite useful in this stage due to their high damage for a low cost.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: At level 36, Octopus Cat can survive, albeit just barely, a hit from Possessed Empress, which allows for it to block her Slowing Mini-Wave. This is crucial for allowing your units to advance and gain back any lost ground.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] and/or [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Both are extremely solid [[Shield Piercing|Shield Piercers]]–Barrel Cat in particular has a way higher proc chance (60%) than Cat Researcher (15%). However, Barrel Cat comes at the cost of being more difficult to obtain, so it really comes down to whichever one the player has.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Amazing for taking out the Shadow Boxer K waves, Pizza Cat can prove valuable for his [[Massive Damage]] and, with his Talents, [[Wave Attack]]s that can pierce into the enemy front lines, dealing valuable chip damage to every peon.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Macho Cat]]: An amazing meatshield for this stage, his 30% chance to [[Dodge]] Dark and Aku attacks makes him very solid for holding ground against the Possessed Empress. His cheap cost and short recharge also allow him to help stall the other non-[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies in the stage.
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: With the Massive Damage VS Dark Talent, C.A.T is a good answer against the Shadow Boxer K and Doge Dark waves, as it's more versatile than Pizza Cat. However, it has lower health, so whereas Pizza Cat will survive a hit from the Possessed Empress, C.A.T. might fall short. Still a unit worth considering regardless.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: With high speed, a guaranteed Shield Pierce and [[Knockback]] and dealing high damage per hit, Supercar Cat is a very potent Shield Piercer that can juggle Possessed Empress easily, though do note its very short range and poor health.

