'''Battle:''' No Shield Piercers this time around: instead, you will be using Esoteric Uril to brute force Possessed Empress's ''12.98 million'' effective HP. Your lineup is entirely dedicated to protecting Uril from the dastardly peons. With all of the Cat Combos in play, Uril is able to survive just long enough for another copy to replace him as he kicks the bucket (assuming he doesn't take external damage).

As soon as the stage begins, upgrade your wallet and lure Doge Dark to the Cat Base. Chip him with two Cat Cactuses, then finish him off with Bullet Train Cat. This lineup is cheap, so after getting out Esoteric Uril, start upgrading your wallet whilst doing your best to babysit Uril. Once you're at a stable income, start sending out King Dragon Cats to aid in killing the non-target enemies. If you're able to outlast the initial horde, then congratulations! The Aku Gories can't do anything to get past your Cat Cactus/Esoteric Uril duo, so your efforts should go into bulldozing every last Shield... one by one. Maybe bring a speed-up for this one if you value your time.

